(C) Structured error rule with Hanni's density: S = S_cheap u S_rand in {0,1}^20, |S| = 1024, p = 2^-10
    S_cheap = {z : z_1..z_11 = 0} (512 points, ~2log11 bits to name), S_rand = 512 random points.
    Three explicit product hypotheses (kappa = 0, B = inf), population risk under uniform inputs:
  good: l = d+19.9, R = 0.01117;  envelope: l = d+28.9, R = 0.00608;  full memoriser: l = d+6420, R = 0
  envelope beats good iff c < 5.717e-04;  full memoriser beats envelope iff c < 9.506e-07; 2^-m = 9.537e-07
  c=1e-05: best of the three = envelope; its average probability of the teacher's error label on E = 0.500
  c=1e-04: best of the three = envelope; its average probability of the teacher's error label on E = 0.500
  c=3e-04: best of the three = envelope; its average probability of the teacher's error label on E = 0.500
  c=1e-03: best of the three = good; its average probability of the teacher's error label on E = 0.001
